    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201196538014_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Soccer (1st Assistant)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-27\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION  Job Title: Assistant Coach- Women’s Soccer (1st Assistant) Department: Athletics Position Reports to (Position Title): Head Coach- Women’s Soccer Effective Date: July 1st, 2026   Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary   Job Description Primary responsibilities are to assist the Head Coach in all aspects of Division I program including, but not limited to, teaching student athletes how to perform soccer, coordinating team travel arrangements, game day personnel management, and other duties as assigned by the Head Coach or Athletic Administration. This position will also assist the Head Coach in organization, administration, and promotion of the program. Approximately 50% of the Assistant Coach’s responsibility is dedicated to the teaching and instruction of Soccer through on-field (or on-court) training and classroom training through use of video and other teaching techniques. Approximately 50% of the Assistant Coach’s responsibilities are other administrative duties. Candidates must be committed to the academic and athletic success of the student-athletes.  Supervisory Responsibilities Graduate Assistants and/or Interns Duties/Responsibilities Assisting with any or all of the following duties as assigned by Head Coach:  TEACHING/INSTRUCTING STUDENT-ATHLETES HOW TO DEVELOP AND PERFORM IN THE SPORT OF SOCCER – Responsible for:  · Instructing players in the rules, regulations, equipment, and techniques of the sport.  · Organizing and directing individual and small group practice activities/exercises as directed by the head coach  · Assess player’s skills, monitors players during competition and practice, and keeps the head coach informed of the athletic performance of students    SCHEDULING– Responsible for:  · Assisting with scheduling of all competition  FINANCIAL AID– Responsible for:  · Understanding NCAA regulations  · Initiating process for initial and renewal grants  · Consistently updating team rosters  · Meeting athletic grant-in-aid budget    BUDGETS– Responsible for:  · Assisting in annual budget preparation  · Staying within amount budgeted for fiscal year  · Having all expenditures pre-approved through appropriate channels    TRAVEL– Responsible for:  · Initiating process for all travel arrangements and submitting reports within 48 hours of return   EQUIPMENT/APPAREL– Responsible for:  · Pre- and Post-season inventory  · Care and maintenance of all equipment/apparel and facilities  · Initiating process to order equipment/apparel    ACADEMICS– Responsible for:  · Supporting all Department of Athletics policies on classroom attendance, study hall, progress reports and enforcing disciplinary actions  · Working with teams to maintain and increase their APR    FUNDRAISING– Responsible for:  · Getting prior approval from the Development office prior to initiating a fund raising activity  · Devising new methods of fund raising  · Being available for Departmental fund raising activities  · Following guidelines established by Department, University, and the NCAA for fund raising activities    PAPERWORK – Responsible for:  · Completing all paperwork by established athletic department and NCAA deadlines    MEETINGS – Responsible for:  · Attending and contributing to all Department of Athletics meetings and requested functions   CAMPS - Responsible for:  · Following guidelines established by Department, University, and the NCAA for camp procedures and operations  RECRUITING - Responsible for:  · Compliance with NCAA recruiting rules and completing associated paperwork in a timely manner · Arranging financially responsible recruiting trips  · Initiating arrangements for all official visits  · Recruiting student who will be an asset to the University and Department of Athletics and graduate in a timely manner   Required Skills/Abilities · Knowledge of NCAA Rules and Regulations · Mastery of sport coached · Ability to lead, guide and direct graduate assistants, interns and student-athletes  · Willingness to form relationships with constituents and help fundraise Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience 1. Minimum Education Requirement:  · Bachelor’s degree from accredited college or university, master’s degree preferred  2. Minimum Work Experience:  · Two years collegiate coaching experience at NCAA Division I level preferred  3. Preferred Qualifications:  · Experience with NCAA Division I Rules and Regulations  · Proven recruiting abilities  · Demonstrated leadership skills Physical Requirements ·Must be able to physically perform essential job duties or have special accommodations arranged in advance Work Conditions · Required to work atypical hours including nights, weekends, potential holidays · May be required to practice in heat, cold, inclement weather Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume with this application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201169687336_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "🌿Guest Artist, LBSCOAS - Application by invitation only.",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-19\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION  Job Title: Guest Artist, LBSCOAS Department: Linda Berry Stein College of Fine Arts & Sciences     Position Reports to: Dean, LNSCOAS Position Class: Exempt (as applicable)   Job Summary - Only individuals invited by the LBS College of Arts and Sciences are eligible to apply. The Guest Artist is a distinguished practitioner invited to contribute specialized artistic/scholastic expertise to the University community. This position enhances the academic experience of students through performances, workshops, masterclasses, lectures, critiques, or short-term instructional engagements. The Guest Artist collaborates with faculty and students to support creative, scholarly, and professional development aligned with the mission of the institution. Duties/Responsibilities Present public performances, exhibitions, readings, lectures, screenings, or demonstrations as scheduled. Conduct masterclasses, workshops, lectures, or direction/rehearsals for students. Provide individual or group critiques and mentorship to students. Collaborate with faculty on curriculum-related activities and special projects. Participate in panel discussions, community outreach, or campus engagement events as requested. Attend rehearsals or preparatory meetings as appropriate. Uphold University policies, procedures, and community standards during the engagement period. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline or equivalent professional experience. Recognized professional achievement in the artistic field. Demonstrated experience in performance, exhibition, or professional artistic practice. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree or terminal degree (MFA, DMA, PhD, or equivalent) in the relevant discipline. Prior experience teaching or working with university students. Regional, national, or international recognition in the field. Experience engaging diverse audiences and academic communities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in a specific discipline (e.g., instrumental/vocal performance, theatre, dance, visual arts, film, creative writing). Ability to engage, inspire, and mentor students. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Professionalism and collaborative approach within an academic environment. Terms of Appointment Appointment is temporary and limited to the duration of the engagement. Compensation will be determined based on scope of services, credentials, and budget approval. Housing, travel, and other expenses may be provided in accordance with University policy and contractual agreement. Work Environment The position may require rehearsal, performance, studio, classroom, or gallery environments. Evening or weekend commitments may be required depending on event scheduling. Only individuals invited by the LBS College of Arts and Sciences are eligible to apply.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9200557661434_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "🌿Campus Safety & Security Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2024-05-16\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nSummary Position Title Campus Safety and Security Officer Department Campus Safety and Security Status Full Time/Non-Exempt Position Summary Patrols University grounds and buildings in order to provide a visible presence to deter crime; respond to all emergencies and routine calls for services in a timely manner and coordinate the police, fire and or medical response to same; Provide general safety information through the daily interaction with the University. Monitor campus special events and parking areas. Dispatch calls and answer Campus Security telephones, assist members of the community who may have questions. Take photo ID pictures and issue identification cards. Issue parking permits and enforce traffic and parking regulations. Position requires minor physical exertion including the consistent need to push, pull, carry, and lift up to 25 pounds on a regular basis and the ability to stand and/or walk for lengthy periods of time without rest or assistance. The Campus Security Officer works within a 24 hour/7 day operation and due to the nature of the position, the Campus Security Officer should expect to work a fluctuating work schedule including holidays, nights and weekends.  Essential Job Duties Serve as a visible and proactive University representative within a 24/7 department charged with providing a secure environment for the University students, affiliates, quests and visitors. Conduct patrols via foot and mountain style bikes to respond to emergencies, provide services and access functions as appropriate, personal escort services. Provide safety awareness through daily contact with the University community and visitors by providing general safety information, directions, parking information. Identify actual or potential safety hazards or conditions and coordinate a resolution with the appropriate department or area. Provide assistance to University personnel in matters involving potential violations to University policy wherein conduct or behavioral expectations are disruptive to the mission of the University. Respond to all emergencies to coordinate law enforcement, medical and/or fire services response to the incident, and to provide a proactive role after the emergency situation has concluded. Make appropriate notifications on campus emergencies as directed. Prepare incident reports and related written communication and maintain activity logs as appropriate. Answer telephones. Dispatch calls via two-way radio. Work special events to provide traffic, parking, and crowd control as needed. Assist the parking program by monitoring parking areas, issuing citations and maintaining access to fire lanes, handicap spaces, and the roadways owned and or controlled by the University. Performs other related duties as assigned by the Director of Campus Security, Coordinator, or assigned Shift Supervisor.  Education and Experience: H.S. Diploma or GED required. A current and valid State of Florida Class D Security Officer License is required. Ability to be creative in developing solutions to complex problems and to multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Ability to provide instruction on personal safety and security issues. Must have a valid driver's license. Must be able to pass a comprehensive background check. Associate Degree is preferred or commensurate experience in the military, law enforcement. or security, preferably on a college campus. Excellent communication skills with a wide variety of people is required. Some typing is required, ability to type 15 wpm. Use of word processing, spreadsheets, database, and email programs required. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested candidates should submit a copy of their resume, cover letter, and list of references with this application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201226537586_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Graduate Prof Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION Job Title: Assistant Director, Graduate and Professional Studies Admission- Recruiter Department: Enrollment Management – Graduate Admissions Position Reports to (Position Title):  Associate Director , Graduate Recruitment Position Class: Exempt Position Type: Full Time/ Primary Position Job Summary The Assistant Director of Graduate and Professions Studies Admissions is responsible for  recruiting, matriculation, academic advising and program management. The Assistant Director will proactively seek out prospective candidates and represent the University at graduate recruitment fairs and events. A successful candidate will have a proven track record of specialized sales, preferably in the professional recruitment of higher education sectors. Looking for self-starting, motivated, relationship-driven, strong communicator who works well independently and with a team Supervisory Responsibilities: •     None Duties/Responsibilities: •     Proactively creates an outbound recruitment strategy to identify and develop new graduate student candidates. •     Provides consultative services to prospective students regarding all details of the programs including application, matriculation, course overviews, program requirements, academic policies and procedures. •     Schedules/hosts official application interviews with each candidate; makes recommendations as part of admissions selection committee. •     Represents Jacksonville University at local and global recruitment fairs. •     Works collaboratively with the Director of Graduate Enrollment Management to address recruitment issues and opportunities while developing comprehensive strategies to achieve annual target enrollment goals. •     Refines and hosts information sessions for prospects and yield events for admitted applicants. •     Supports the development and utilization of recruiting management system; especially to build a strong communication flow for prospective and matriculated students. Develops and maintains cooperative relationships with other schools and universities. •     Provides expertise on recruitment strategies to marketing team •     Perform other relevant duties as assigned Required Skills/Abilities: •     Specialized and relationship-based sales and/or recruiting experience with proven track record of achieving goals. •     Able to develop, plan and achieve short and long-range goals. •     Strong analytical and problem-solving skills; ability to evaluate data, assess alternatives and make appropriate decisions/recommendations. •     Strong interpersonal and communication skills, including oral, written; especially for presentations. •     Demonstrates tact and diplomacy, maintaining a high level of confidentiality. •     Strong organizational, time management and project-management skills. •     Motivated to work independently but able to thrive and contribute in a team-oriented environment •     Computer proficiency in MS Office Suite, Google and other basic software Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: •     Master’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience •     Experience working in a graduate academic setting, in a business school, with students who are professional working adults, and/or with international students is preferred. •     Experience with higher education recruitment and admission preferred Physical Requirements: •     Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. •     Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. •     Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. •     Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201228374579_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Simulationist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION  Job Title: Simulationist  Department: Keigwin School of Nursing and  Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences Position Reports to (Position Title): Director of Simulation and Department Chair of Simulation Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time Is this a Primary or Additional Position: Primary   Job Summary Facilitate the daily operations of the Keigwin School of Nursing (KSON) Simulation Training and Applied Research (STAR) Center and Clinical Skills Lab under the direction of the Simulation Director and Department Chair. The Simulation Center and Clinical Skills Lab are environments that support critical thinking and experiential learning experiences for KSON students, Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences (BRCHS) students, and community partners. The simulationist will participate in the delivery of clinical simulation experiences and the operation of manikin simulators or standardized patients (SPs) to be used effectively in healthcare education and training. Duties/Responsibilities Collaborate with the Director of the Simulation, the Department Chair of Simulation, KSON faculty, BRCHS faculty, and community partners to maximize the utilization of clinical learning in simulation centers Collaborate and implement current evidence-based practice in simulation learning set by the International Nursing Association for Clinical Simulation and Learning (INACSL) Organize and execute the set-up and breakdown of equipment, supplies, and materials for scheduled courses and simulations in the lab and classrooms. This includes standardized patient and simulators moulage. Operate simulation software and audiovisual equipment Collect and analyze lab survey responses for assigned courses to determine the effectiveness of simulation on student learning, critical thinking, and clinical decision- making. Discuss the findings with the Simulation Director to identify potential improvements. Assist in the operation of manikin simulators and Standardized Patients (SPs) to facilitate their use in healthcare education and training Develop and create ways to enhance learning in the lab, such as facilitating lunch and learns, and other coordinated activities Provide for the general cleanliness and security of the laboratory. Appropriate disposal of hazardous materials for OSHA standards. Collaborate with the Simulation Director to engage faculty & community partners in developing, implementing, and evaluating courses, simulation scenarios, simulation tools, and other educational initiatives to promote and measure student learning outcomes Communicate and collaborate in a positive, professional manner with the Director of the Simulation, Department Chair of Simulation, faculty, simulationists, and IT operation specialists Collaborate with Simulation Operations and IT specialists to maintain, troubleshoot, and resolve issues related to the operation and maintenance of simulation equipment. Participate in grant and contractual-related activities as designated by the Director of Simulation Remain current with developments in the field of simulation technology and learning theory. Maintain records of experiential learning activities in an electronic database Participate in professional development and attend professional meetings and conferences Attend regularly scheduled JU KSON meetings and activities as appropriate Participate in simulation meetings for the STAR Center and Skills Lab Participate in KSON organization committee(s) Serve as a mentor and role model for students in the lab Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities Excellent communication skills (both verbal and written) Technologically inclined and proficient in Microsoft applications Familiar with the healthcare environment and operations, proficient in medical terminology, and well-versed in clinical practices.  Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills Innovative Best Practice simulation implementation and use of simulation technology. Ability to work collaboratively with the simulation team, Jacksonville University faculty and staff, and interdisciplinary community partners. May travel between campus buildings or off-campus. Able to work with self-initiative and autonomy. Simulation experience preferred. Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience:  A bachelor's degree from an accredited institution is required. A degree in nursing or other healthcare related field preferred. Previous simulation experience.  Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator or Operator preferred or a desire to work towards it. Physical Recquirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone. No limitations on physical lifting ability of simulation manikins and equipment up to 80 lbs. with assistance.  No Latex Allergy.  Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.   To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume along with a JU application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201231519524_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "KSON Nursing Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION  Job Title:   KSON Nursing Programs Coordinator & Social Media Content Creator  Department:  Keigwin School of Nursing Position Reports to (Position Title):  Director of Entry Level Programs and Associate Dean of Nursing Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt): Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time): Full Time    Job Summary This position assists the Entry and Advanced Level-Directors of the Keigwin School of Nursing. It requires the incumbent to assume responsibility for a variety of activities related to the operationalizing the various nursing programs. This position works in collaboration with nursing faculty and other administrative personnel in the Keigwin School of Nursing. Supervisor Responsibilities Student workers  Duties/Responsibilities Administrative Support and Communications Provides administrative support to program directors Serves as the primary point of contact for visitors to the KSON building and for communication with Nursing Program Directors. Communicates building-related information, submits work orders, and ensures compliance with safety protocols. Attends committee meetings within KSON as assigned by Program Directors Scheduling and Operational Management Maintains the master schedule for all KSON programs, including faculty load assignments, adjunct and overload scheduling, and classroom coordination Manages daily operational activities for the KSON, including updates to the website, distribution of student announcements, and oversight of social media platforms. Manages and schedules conference rooms within the BRCHS building. Oversees the scheduling, task assignment, and supervision of student workers in alignment with the goals of KSON leadership. Assists with the creation, management, and maintenance of KSON policies and procedures in collaboration with Directors and the Associate Dean. Student Engagement and Events Assists in planning and implementing student activities and KSON events in collaboration with KSON leadership and faculty Develops, organizes, and maintains nursing student engagement projects. Serves as a liaison for nursing student tours and the entry-level nursing program ambassador program. Coordinates with Nursing Program Directors to assess and support student needs. Marketing and Social Media Collaborates with the Department Chair of Online, Cohorts, and Marketing to manage KSON’s social media presence Creates, posts, and advertises events on social media platforms in alignment with the KSON mission and policies. Monitors social media accounts and responds to comments in a professional and timely manner. Data and Reporting Assists in the aggregation of program data and preparation of reports.  Other Performs other duties as assigned to support the mission and operations of the Keigwin School of Nursing. Required Skills/Abilities Excellent communication skills (both veral and written) Understanding of and commitment to the use of technology Proficiency in social media applications, especially Facebook and Twitter Proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Microsoft Word and Excel Strong organizational skills Event planning Customer-focused approach Education, Experience, Licenses & Certifications Bachelor’s degree Master's Degree (preferred) Knowledge of nursing profession and educational requirements, experience in advising preferred Experience working in a diverse environment Preferred: experience working in organization systems management and/or leadership Preferred: experience working in a university environment. Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone No limitations on physical lifting ability   Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.  To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume, cover letter, list of references with a JU application.",
