    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201235151075_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Asso. Dir. UG Admis Student Engage Recruitmen",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Associate Director, UG Admissions-Student Engagement and Recruitment Department: Enrollment Management-Undergraduate Admissions  Position Reports to (Position Title): Director, Undergraduate Recruitment  Position Class/Position Type: Exempt, Full-Time Primary or Additional Position: Primary   Job Summary The Associate Director of UG Admissions – Student Engagement & Recruitment is responsible for leading undergraduate student recruitment and enrollment efforts for Jacksonville University in Florida and throughout the Southeast, with a particular focus on local recruitment and community engagement. The Associate Director will lead the development and implementation of recruitment and student engagement initiatives, build and maintain professional relationships with prospective students and key internal and external partners, and manage recruitment efforts across multiple mediums and venues, including in-person events, virtual platforms, social media, and other relationship-management tools. The Associate Director will manage and support a team of admissions counselors, provide guidance throughout the recruitment and enrollment process, and collaborate with university partners to strengthen internal recruitment and engagement efforts. The position will also evaluate applications and supporting documentation, advise prospective students through the admissions and enrollment process, and identify opportunities to improve conversion and enrollment outcomes. The Associate Director will monitor key recruitment and enrollment metrics, assess progress toward enrollment goals throughout the admissions cycle, and use data and market insights to inform recruitment strategies and priorities. This position will play a key role in strengthening Jacksonville University’s presence in the local and regional markets while supporting broader institutional enrollment objectives and will make recommendations to university leadership regarding recruitment strategy, market opportunities, and initiatives to support enrollment growth. Supervisory Resonsibilities: Interviews, hires and trains new staff. Oversees the daily workflow of the department. Evaluates staff performance and provides timely feedback. Helps to resolve employee issues and disputes. Handles discipline and termination of employees in accordance with university policy.   Duties/Responsibilities:  Communicate and provide support to prospective students, applicants, parents, advisors, consultants, recruiting partners, and other stakeholders to facilitate the admissions and enrollment process and provide a high level of service. Manage, train, develop, and support a team of admissions counselors, providing guidance and direction to ensure effective recruitment and student engagement practices. Ensure accurate and timely maintenance of recruitment records, data, and reporting related to local and assigned-territory recruitment activities and outcomes. Analyze current and historical enrollment trends in assigned territories, with particular attention to the local Jacksonville market, to develop recruitment strategies that support the University’s enrollment goals. Develop and implement goals, projects, and strategies that strengthen Jacksonville University’s local internal and external relationships and leverage community partnerships to support enrollment goals. Make recommendations to the Director of Undergraduate Recruitment and the Vice President of Enrollment Management regarding admissions processes, recruitment initiatives, local market opportunities, and strategies to support enrollment growth. Cultivate and explore new relationships, partnerships, and networks that can enhance local recruitment efforts and increase Jacksonville University’s visibility within the community. Make individual and large- or small-group presentations to prospective students, families, school counselors, community partners, and other audiences regarding Jacksonville University and its academic programs. Collaborate with internal University departments to research, collect, analyze, and share information and data relevant to the local marketplace, recruitment activities, and enrollment opportunities. Integrate vendor partnerships and utilize current undergraduate recruitment resources to enhance student engagement, recruitment efforts, and the overall resources available to prospective students throughout the admissions cycle. Provide recommendations to University leadership regarding local and regional recruitment strategy, emerging market trends, partnership opportunities, and initiatives that may strengthen student recruitment and enrollment. Provide excellent customer service and maintain a student-centered approach in every aspect of the role. Work autonomously, demonstrate initiative and proactive problem-solving, and make ethical and sound decisions in support of University and enrollment objectives. Performs other duties as assigned.   Required Skills/Abilities:  Flexibility and adaptability Collaborative, supportive leader and teammate Excellent organization and project management skills Excellent communication and customer service skills Demonstrated tech savviness and ability to learn and operate different systems. Person of character, drive and integrity who will always represent the University in a professional manner Ability to meet appropriate situation with reasonable, creative responses to achieve the goals and objectives of the recruitment effort Dedicated to the mission of Jacksonville University regarding the growth of its student population   Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience:  Bachelor’s required, in any field 3+ years working in enrollment management, preferably in undergraduate admissions 1+ years managerial experience Strong understanding of the admissions cycle, application review process, student recruitment, and key industry metrics Experience developing and implementing strategic initiatives and planning recruitment travel Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite, Google, and other basic technology; Experience with Technolutions Slate preferred   Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 20 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines. Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone.   Important Note   This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.     To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume and cover letter with a JU application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201235431283_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Office Associate, Social Sciences & Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-17\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nPosition Title: Office Associate -  School of Social Science & Education, Department of Humanities, and College of Law Department: Linda Berry Stein College of Arts & Sciences Position Reports to: Dean of Linda Berry Stein College of Arts & Sciences Position Type:   Full-Time, Exempt Position Summary:  This position is responsible for providing administrative support to the School of Social Sciences and Education. The Department of Humanities, and the College of Law. The position is full-time and shared between Social Sciences, Education, Humanities, College of Law, and the stein College of Arts & Sciences.  Supervisory Responsibilities: The position hires, reviews, supervises, and terminates student workers.  Duties/Responsibilities:  -Provide administrative support to the Director of Social Sciences & Education, Chair of Humanities, Chair of Education, the College of Law, and the students and faculty within these divisions. -Assist with administrative duties including record keeping, work orders, purchase requests, invoice tracking, PCard purchases, processing mail, maintaining copiers, maintaining buildings (Gooding, Council, and Founders buildings), onboarding adjuncts, hiring and supervising student workers. -Submit key requests, name badge orders, and office supply requests for new faculty. Provide administrative support for new full-time and adjunct faculty. -Manage the organization of events including catering, 25 Live, invitations, tracking attendance, decorations, and other details as needed per event. -Collaborate with Chairs to create and submit Payroll Sheets each semester. -Assist faculty in arranging field trips and professional development travel arrangements. -Foster and maintain a professional and friendly office environment, including assisting students and visitors with directions and with faculty or department contact information, and maintaining organized and clean offices and supply rooms. -Monitor website pages for any needed updates. -Coordinate faculty search campus visits by creating the daily interview schedules and working with the Director of College Operations to ensure hotel, travel, and Dean’s availability -Other duties as assigned by the Dean’s Office Education and Experience:   Minimum Education Requirement: High school diploma Minimum Work Experience: - 2+ years in a professional office environment providing administrative support Advanced Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Office skills Customer service experience  Preferred Qualifications:  -Superior written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills with a strong dedication to customer service. -Experience working with multiple teams and in a higher education environment. -Demonstrated proactive problem-solving skills and ability to work under stress and time pressures. -Strong organizational, time management, and communication skills. -Ability to set priorities, make timely decisions, and meet deadlines while working on multiple projects. -Possess high standards of ethics, accuracy, and precision. -Ability to think creatively, highly driven, and self-motivated. -Knowledge of basic bookkeeping/accounts payable principles. Physical Requirements: - Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 40 lbs. -Must be able to stoop, bend, and reach -Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines -Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens -Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Work Conditions -Work is primarily indoors, but requires the employee to be in an outdoor environment when traveling between campus buildings or being off-campus -Standard office hours are 8:30 am to 5:00 pm -Employee will be exposed to frequent noise caused by telephones, operating functions, and office machines Important Note: This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. Acknowledgment: Submission of my application acknowledges receipt and understanding of this job description. I verify that I am capable of and willing to fulfill all essential functions of this position. I am willing to be flexible and willing to do various jobs that are not listed, as the need arises.",
