    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9205249650372_2&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Help Desk Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Help Desk Specialist Department : Information Technology Position Reports to: Interim CIO Position Class/Type :   Exempt/Full-Time Job Summary  The Help Desk Specialist is the first point of contact for employees who need technical help. You will resolve hardware, software, account and network issues by phone, email, chat and in person. The position will be responsible for generating tickets in the Help Desk system for customer requests/issues and assigning them appropriately; providing configuration and training support for university standard software packages; assisting Faculty/Staff with computer software and hardware questions. Success in this role means fast, friendly fixes, clear documentation, and users who feel heard. The Help Desk Specialist will work in person on Jacksonville University’s campus, supporting students, faculty and staff.   Supervisory Responsibilities:  None  Duties/Responsibilities: Respond to support requests by phone, email, chat and walk-up, and log request in the ticketing system. Diagnose and resolve Tier 1 issues with desktops, laptops, mobile devices, printers and peripherals. Support user accounts: password resets, MFA enrollment Troubleshoot basic network connectivity, including Wi-Fi, VPN, and network drive access. Support Microsoft 365: email, Teams, OneDrive etc. Escalate complex issues to team members through TDX with complete notes, and follow them through to resolution. Write and update knowledge base articles and how-to guides for users and fellow technicians. Meet service-level targets for response and resolution time, and keep users updated on ticket status. Follow security policies: verify identity before account changes, spot and report phishing, and protect sensitive data.    Required Skills/Abilities: Customer focus  — patient, courteous and calm with frustrated users. Problem solving  — methodical troubleshooting that isolates root causes rather than symptoms. Communication  — explains technical steps in plain language and writes clear ticket notes. Organization  — juggles multiple tickets, prioritizes by business impact and follows up on time. Learning agility  — picks up new tools and systems quickly and shares what they learn. Integrity  — handles confidential data and privileged access responsibly. Teamwork  — collaborates with IT Team, other departments and vendors.   Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: Minimum Education Requirement:  Technical degree, certificates, or equivalent experience Minimum Work Experience:  Help Desk experience, IT experience Preferred Education Qualification:  Associate's or bachelor's degree in IT, computer science or a related field Preferred Qualitfications: Excellent communication skills (written, verbal, and listening) Certifications such as CompTIA A+, Network+, Microsoft 365 Fundamentals / etc   W ork Environment: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 30 pounds Must be able to bend, stoop and reach Must be able to sit or stand for extended periods of time Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines   Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 40 pounds Must be able to bend, stoop and reach Must able to sit or stand for extended periods of time Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. Benefits and Perks of Life @ JU All Full Time Positions: Generous paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, jury duty, and bereavement leave  Paid Federal Holidays  Additional time off for Thanksgiving, Winter holidays, and Spring Break  FSA/HSA eligibility  Retirement plan with a dollar-for-dollar University match of up to 6% following the vesting period  Robust health benefits (medical, dental, vision)  100% Employer-Sponsored benefits: Short Term Disability (buy-up option available), Long Term Disability, Employee Assistance Program, Life Insurance, Parent Leave  Additional benefit options: Accident coverage, Pet Insurance, Legal, Critical Illness, Dependent Life  Tuition benefits for employees, spouses, and dependent children up to 26 years of age  Domestic Partner benefit eligibility  Veteran and Military Service Support Program  Discounted on-campus dining meal plans; 2 free meals per week during Fall and Spring semesters  Monthly wellness initiatives  Service awards & Recognition programs  10% discounts at the on-campus JU Bookstore, School of Orthodontics  Free Microsoft Office downloads to personal computers/devices  Free on-campus parking  Access to campus amenities, including the fitness center, resort-style pool, and library  Disclaimer: Benefits and time-off programs are subject to eligibility requirements and may vary based on position and employment status",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9205250783150_3&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Full/Associate Professor of Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-31\n\nJob Title: Associate/Full Professor of Law Department: College of Law Position Reports to:  Dean, College of Law Effective Date:  2027/2028 Academic Year Salary:  commensurate with qualifications and experience Position Type/Class:   Exempt, Full-Time About Jacksonville University and the College of Law   Jacksonville University is a premier private institution in northeast Florida. Founded in 1934, JU offers more than 100 majors, minors, and programs to more than 2,000 undergraduate and 1,000 graduate students. The University combines the strengths of a comprehensive institution with the close faculty-student engagement of a small university. Founded in 2022, the Jacksonville University College of Law received provisional approval from the American Bar Association in 2024. The College is building a student-centered law school committed to academic excellence, professional formation, and service to Jacksonville and northeast Florida. Faculty members have a meaningful role in shaping the curriculum, institutional policies, scholarly culture, and traditions of a growing law school. The College of Law is located in a dedicated facility in the heart of downtown Jacksonville, within walking distance of state and federal courts, City Hall, government law offices, legal services organizations, and many of the region's leading law firms. This setting supports strong partnerships with the bench, bar, public agencies, and broader community and creates distinctive opportunities for experiential learning and professional engagement. Jacksonville is a vibrant and growing coastal city with a diverse economy, an active legal community, and abundant opportunities for outdoor recreation. Job Summary   Jacksonville University College of Law invites applications from lateral candidates for one or more full-time, tenured faculty positions for the 2027-2028 academic year. Appointments may be made at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, depending on the successful candidate's qualifications and experience. The College has particular interest in candidates prepared to teach bar preparation, including JU's required three-credit bar preparation course; legal writing; Contracts; Corporations; and other transactional courses. Because the College expects to grow its faculty substantially over the next several years, however, applications are welcome from candidates in all areas of expertise. Flexibility to teach across the curriculum will be highly valued, as will experience with the ABA accreditation process and enthusiasm for the opportunities and responsibilities of building a new law school. The successful candidate will teach courses assigned in light of curricular needs and the candidate's expertise; maintain a productive scholarly agenda; advise and mentor students; participate actively in faculty governance and institutional service; and contribute to the College's academic program, professional community, and continued development. Faculty members are also expected to support the University's mission and to engage constructively with colleagues, students, alumni, members of the profession, and community partners. This is an in-person faculty position. Faculty members are expected to maintain a regular and substantial on-campus presence during the academic year and to participate in person in teaching, advising, faculty governance, College programming, and other institutional responsibilities. The successful candidate must reside in the Jacksonville metropolitan area, or within a reasonable commuting distance of the College of Law, by the beginning of the appointment. This position is not eligible for a fully remote work arrangement. Qualifications Applicants must hold a J.D. or equivalent law degree. Candidates must demonstrate a record of excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Relevant considerations may include academic record, professional experience, scholarly achievement, teaching experience and effectiveness, and the ability to contribute to the College's mission and institutional development. Candidates should demonstrate accomplishments appropriate to the desired rank. Jacksonville University’s Policy on Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and virtually Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Stamina to teach up to 24 hours weekly How to Apply Applications should include (1) a cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, and (3) a list of three professional references. Candidates may also submit other materials they would like the committee to consider, such as a scholarly agenda, writing sample, teaching statement, syllabi, or teaching evaluations. Applications and questions may be emailed to lawhiring@ju.edu. All candidates invited to interview will also be asked to submit application materials through the Jacksonville University employment portal . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position or positions are filled. Diversity and Inclusion Jacksonville University, an Equal Opportunity Employer, believes students learn best in a diverse and inclusive community and is committed to academic excellence through diversity among its faculty, staff, and students. We seek candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports the growth and development of a diverse student body. We strongly encourage applications from people of color, women, LGBTQ+ people, veterans, and others whose backgrounds and life experiences would contribute to the diversity of our faculty and law school community. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201236572556_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION  Job Title:  Assistant Professor of Engineering Department:  David College of Business & Technology Position Reports to (Position Title):  Director of Technology and the Dean of DCOBT Effective Date:  July 1 ,  2027   Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt):  Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time):  Full-time, 9-month Faculty, Tenure Track Is this a Primary or Additional Position:  Primary   Job Summary Full-time faculty members at Jacksonville University are expected to teach undergraduate and/or graduate classes, conduct scholarship and engage in professional development activities, and complete university and/or community service. The position will be a full-time, 9-month contract, tenure track position. Supervisory Responsibilities Most faculty positions do not have supervisory responsibilities Some may have supervisory responsibilities when the faculty member is serving in a Director or Associate Dean position for additional compensation and or release time. This will be specified in the contract. Duties/Responsibilities Teach classes—a typical load is 24 hours annually Engage in research/scholarship Supervise student research projects Supervise student internships Participate in university service at the department, school, college, or university level Participate in community service (optional) Required Skills/Abilities The ability to teach a broad range of lower-level and upper-level courses The ability to incorporate technology into classroom teaching and to teach online and hybrid classes The ability to supervise and conduct research and supervise student research in area of expertise The ability to work with diverse students and small class sizes Participation in departmental, school, college, or university service Excellent oral and written skills Time management and organizational skills The ability to work in a collaborative and cooperative manner Education and Experience Typically, terminal degree in area of expertise Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and virtually. Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Stamina to teach up to 24 hours weekly. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.  To Apply Please submit your cover letter and resume/CV with your JU application.",
