    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201230796538_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION  Job Title:  Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Department:  Keigwin School of Nursing Position Reports to (Position Title):  Associate Dean & Director of Nursing, Undergraduate Position Class (Exempt or Non-Exempt):  Exempt Position Type (Full Time or Part Time):  Full Time    Job Summary Jacksonville University invites applicants for a PMHNP faculty position in the Keigwin School of Nursing. This is a clinical track, full time, 12-month position. This position is in classroom with assignments in mental health and advanced practice nursing. Supervisory Responsibilities None Duties/Responsibilities Graduate teaching : Deliver instruction to graduate and doctoral nursing students across ground-based, online, and hybrid formats, as well as advanced clinical simulation labs. Curriculum instruction : Teach advanced psychopharmacology, advanced pathophysiology/neurobiology, psychiatric diagnostic reasoning, and evidence-based psychotherapy across the lifespan. Clinical scholarship : Maintain active PMHNP clinical practice, participate in professional organizations, and chair DNP capstone projects and graduate research. Institutional service : Contribute to university committees, community mental health partnerships, student mentoring, and campus events. Simulation design : Create advanced psychiatric simulations, standardized patient encounters, and telehealth scenarios for graduate cohorts. Safety integration : Embed evidence-based suicide risk assessments, psychotropic medication safety protocols, de-escalation practices, and legal/ethical mandates into simulation exercises. Curricular coordination : Collaborate with faculty colleagues to thread psychiatric- mental health competencies throughout the graduate nursing curriculum. Competency evaluation : Assess clinical diagnostic formulations, therapeutic communication, and guided self-reflection during post-simulation debriefings. Clinical facilitation : Lead psychiatric interviewing labs, case formulation exercises, and structured clinical debriefings. Committee service : Serve on the Keigwin School of Nursing Graduate Committee and PMHNP academic review panels. Clinical Facilitation: Lead psychiatric interviewing labs, case formulation exercises, and structured clinical debriefings. Certification support : Provide academic coaching in clinical prioritization, diagnostic reasoning, stress management, and national PMHNP certification exam preparation (such as ANCC). Educational innovation : Stay current with emerging psychiatric simulation technologies, telehealth modalities, and adult learning theories. Professional development : Maintain APRN licensure, national PMHNP board certification, and active attendance at regional and national nursing conferences. Faculty governance : Attend scheduled Keigwin School of Nursing faculty meetings and graduate assembly activities. Program recruitment : Participate in applicant interviews, open houses, and community outreach for the PMHNP program. Related duties : Fulfill additional academic, clinical, and administrative responsibilities as assigned. Required Skills/Abilities Unencumbered Florida APRN license Certification and practice experience as a PMHNP Instruct, professionally communicate, and demonstrate nursing skills techniques to nursing students. Self-directed, have computer proficiency that includes the knowledge necessary to develop case scenarios and simulations. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to evaluate nursing students in the teaching/learning lab environment. Knowledge of effective teaching techniques and curriculum development. Skill in facilitating development of student problem solving skills. Ability to design effective learning activities for students. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff. Role model professionalism and maintain professional skills lab environment for students. Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience DNP or PhD in Nursing PMHNP certification and licensing Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Able to lift and turn objects up to 90 lbs. without physical restrictions. Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.   To Apply Interested candidates are asked to submit a resume, cover letter, and list of references with this application.",
