    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201229034835_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Visiting Clinical Assistant Prof, Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Description Job title: Visiting Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Department: Brooks Rehabilitation College of Healthcare Sciences, Keigwin School of Nursing Position Reports to (Position Title): Associate Dean of Nursing, Undergraduate Job summary Jacksonville University invites applicants for a faculty position in the Keigwin School of Nursing. This is a visiting, clinical track, full time, 12-month position that involves in-person, classroom instruction. Supervisory Responsibilities: None Duties/Responsibilities Teaching will include undergraduate students in ground-based and hybrid models. Teaching also extends into the skills lab environment. Primary areas of instruction include Med-surg, pathophysiology, assessment and synthesis. Scholarship to include clinical practice, attendance at professional meetings and chairing of UG research and/or doctoral projects. University service to include committee membership, special projects, community activities, mentoring, attendance, and support for university events. Collaborate, revise, and deliver simulation learning experiences for graduate and undergraduate nursing students. Integrate and teach EB practice, current medical errors, practice, and safety mandates into simulation practice scenarios in the lab setting. Collaborate and coordinate faculty to promote and infuse simulation throughout curriculum. Evaluate students' learning and skill acquisition and integrate guided reflection into post- simulation debriefings. Facilitate and implement teaching scenario/learning situations of nursing skills, simulations, and debriefing sessions. Serve on Keigwin School of Nursing Undergraduate committee. Facilitate available resources for students with study skills, priority setting, and test taking skills, including NCLEX-RN test taking strategies and time/stress management. Remain current with developments in the field of simulation technology and learning theory. Participate in professional development and attend professional meetings. Attend regularly scheduled JU Keigwin School of Nursing general faculty meetings and activities. Participate in recruitment and public relation activities of the Keigwin School of Nursing.  Perform other related duties as assigned.  Required Skills/Abilites Unencumbered Florida RN license Instruct, professionally communicate, and demonstrate nursing skills techniques to nursing students. Self-directed, have computer proficiency that includes the knowledge necessary to develop case scenarios and simulations. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to evaluate nursing students in the teaching/learning lab environment. Knowledge of effective teaching techniques and curriculum development. Skill in facilitating development of student problem solving skills. Ability to design effective learning activities for students. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff. Role model professionalism and maintain professional skills lab environment for students. Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience   MSN in Nursing Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Able to lift and turn objects up to 90 lbs. without physical restrictions. Important Note   This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. To Apply Interested applicants are asked to submit a resume, cover letter, and list of references with a JU application.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9201221986103_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title:  Assistant/Associate Professor of Law Department:   College of Law Position Reports to: Dean of College of Law Position Type:  Full-Time, Exempt About Jacksonville University and the College of Law Jacksonville University is a premier private institution in northeast Florida. Founded in 1934, JU offers more than 100 majors, minors, and programs to more than 2,000 undergraduate and 1,000 graduate students. The University combines the strengths of a comprehensive institution with the close faculty-student engagement of a small university. Founded in 2022, the Jacksonville University College of Law received provisional approval from the American Bar Association in 2024. The College is building a student-centered law school committed to academic excellence, professional formation, and service to Jacksonville and northeast Florida. Faculty members have a meaningful role in shaping the curriculum, institutional policies, scholarly culture, and traditions of a growing law school. The College of Law is located in a dedicated facility in the heart of downtown Jacksonville, within walking distance of state and federal courts, City Hall, government law offices, legal services organizations, and many of the region's leading law firms. This setting supports strong partnerships with the bench, bar, public agencies, and broader community and creates distinctive opportunities for experiential learning and professional engagement. Jacksonville is a vibrant and growing coastal city with a diverse economy, an active legal community, and abundant opportunities for outdoor recreation. Job Summary Jacksonville University College of Law invites applications from entry-level and lateral candidates for one or more full-time, tenure-track faculty positions for the 2026-2027 academic year. Appointments may be made at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor, depending on the successful candidate's qualifications and experience. The College has particular interest in candidates prepared to teach bar preparation, including JU's required three-credit bar preparation course; legal writing; Contracts; Corporations; and other transactional courses. Because the College expects to grow its faculty substantially over the next several years, however, applications are welcome from candidates in all areas of expertise. Flexibility to teach across the curriculum will be highly valued, as will experience with the ABA accreditation process and enthusiasm for the opportunities and responsibilities of building a new law school. The successful candidate will teach courses assigned in light of curricular needs and the candidate's expertise; develop and maintain a productive scholarly agenda; advise and mentor students; participate actively in faculty governance and institutional service; and contribute to the College's academic program, professional community, and continued development. Faculty members are also expected to support the University's mission and to engage constructively with colleagues, students, alumni, members of the profession, and community partners. This is an in-person faculty position. Faculty members are expected to maintain a regular and substantial on-campus presence during the academic year and to participate in person in teaching, advising, faculty governance, College programming, and other institutional responsibilities. The successful candidate must reside in the Jacksonville metropolitan area, or within a reasonable commuting distance of the College of Law, by the beginning of the appointment. This position is not eligible for a fully remote work arrangement. Qualifications Applicants must hold a J.D. or equivalent law degree. Tenure-track candidates must demonstrate, or show strong promise of, excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Relevant considerations may include academic record, professional experience, scholarly potential or achievement, teaching experience and effectiveness, and the ability to contribute to the College's mission and institutional development. Candidates whose experience warrants appointment at the rank of Associate Professor should demonstrate accomplishments appropriate to that rank. Candidates who prefer a non-tenure-track position focused primarily on teaching and service may indicate that interest in their cover letter. How to Apply Applications should include (1) a cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, and (3) a list of three professional references. Candidates may also submit other materials they would like the committee to consider, such as a scholarly agenda, writing sample, teaching statement, syllabi, or teaching evaluations. Applications and questions may be emailed to lawhiring@ju.edu. All candidates invited to interview will also be asked to submit application materials through the Jacksonville University employment portal . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position or positions are filled. Diversity and Inclusion Jacksonville University, an Equal Opportunity Employer, believes students learn best in a diverse and inclusive community and is committed to academic excellence through diversity among its faculty, staff, and students. We seek candidates who will contribute to a climate that supports the growth and development of a diverse student body. We strongly encourage applications from people of color, women, LGBTQ+ people, veterans, and others whose backgrounds and life experiences would contribute to the diversity of our faculty and law school community. Jacksonville University’s Policy on Physical Requirements Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and other business machines Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and virtually Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Stamina to teach up to 24 hours weekly  Important Note This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, and/or skills required for this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs. Acknowledgment Submission of an application acknowledges receipt and understanding of this job description. I verify that I am capable of and willing to fulfill all essential functions of this position. I am willing to be flexible and willing to do various jobs that are not listed, as the need arises.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=77bf9053-07ed-47ba-b601-d78b61854199&ccId=9200563802212_2&jobId=9200911832245_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology & Marine Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-07-16\n\nLocation: Jacksonville\n\nJob Title: Assistant Professor Department: Biology & Marine Science Position Reports to: Chair of Biology & Marine Science Department Effective Date: January 1, 2026 Job Summary Jacksonville University invites applications for a non-tenured track Assistant Professor of Biology  and Marine Science beginning in January 2026. The Department of Biology and Marine Science is seeking a marine vertebrate biologist with research interests in the fields of elasmobranch, marine mammal or sea turtle biology, ecology, and/or population dynamics. A specific focus in genetics, sensory biology, physiology, modeling, and/or GIS in research is preferred although other areas will be considered. The candidate must be qualified to teach undergraduate and graduate courses related to their area of research as well as introductory marine biology courses. Further, they must be able to teach online courses at the master’s degree level to support the MA/MS in Marine Science and MS in Marine Studies graduate programs. Teaching and research activities should encompass a combination of both field and laboratory activities. Successful candidates are expected to: 1) have a strong commitment to providing high-quality education with significant teacher/student interaction, 2) develop active grant-funded research involving undergraduates and graduate students, and 3) participate in Department, School, College, and University service. A Ph.D. or DVM is required by the time of appointment.  Jacksonville University, an Equal Opportunity Employer, believes students learn best in a diverse, inclusive community and is therefore committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. We seek candidates who are committed to Jacksonville University’s efforts to create a climate that fosters the growth and development of a diverse student body, and we actively welcome applications from members of groups who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Jacksonville University is a comprehensive, liberal arts college located in Jacksonville, FL, a diverse metropolitan community with a thriving economic and cultural scene. Jacksonville International Airport provides easy access to US and international destinations. The College emphasizes innovative and quality teaching in small classes and ranks in the annual rankings of “America’s Best Colleges,” released by U.S. News & World Report. Please visit our website at www.ju.edu . Duties/Responsibilities: Teach classes with a typical load of 24 hours annually. Develop an active research program related to the field of study. Supervise undergraduate and graduate student research projects, internships, and other scholarly activities. Participate in service at the department, school, college, and university level Required Skills/Abilities: Expected area of teaching, research, and mentorship, emphasis is in the field of marine vertebrate  biology. An ability to teach marine science courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Must be able to teach online courses at the master’s degree level to support the graduate programs. Education, Certificates, Licenses, and Experience: Ph.D. in Marine Science or other related discipline or DVM Undergraduate teaching experience in Marine Science is strongly preferred. Physical Requirements: Manual dexterity to efficiently operate a computer keyboard and scientific equipment. Adequate  hearing to communicate effectively in person and virtually. Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Stamina to teach  up to 24 hours weekly. Combination of work indoors and outdoors Some off-campus travel may be required. Work is performed under minimum supervision and requires incumbent to exercise independence and discretion. Application Components A current curriculum vitae Letter of Interest outlining relevant experience matching the requested skills/attributes of the  candidate Three Letters of Recommendation. Application Close: September 1st, 2025 Benefits and Perks of Life @ JU Generalized/All Full Time Positions: Generous paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, jury duty, and bereavement leave Paid Federal Holidays  Additional time off for Thanksgiving, Winter holidays, and SpringBreak FSA/HSA eligibility  Retirement plan with a dollar-for-dollar University match of up to 6% following the vesting period Robust health benefits (medical, dental, vision) 100% Employer-Sponsored benefits: Short Term Disability (buy-up option available), Long Term Disability, Employee Assistance Program, Life Insurance, Parent Leave  Additional benefit options: Accident coverage, Pet Insurance, Legal, Critical Illness, Dependent Life Tuition benefits for employees, spouses, and dependent children up to26 years of age Domestic Partner benefit eligibility   Veteran and Military Service Support Program  Discounted on-campus dining meal plans; 2 free meals per week during Fall and Spring semesters  Monthly wellness initiatives Service awards & Recognition programs  10% discounts at the on-campus JU Bookstore, School of Orthodontics Free Microsoft Office downloads to personal computers/devices  Free on-campus parking  Access to campus amenities, including the fitness center, resort-style pool, and library Disclaimer: Benefits and time-off programs are subject to eligibility requirements and may vary based on position and employment status.  Important Note This  is  not  an  exhaustive  list  of all  responsibilities, duties,  and/or  skills  required   for  this position. The University reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet organizational needs.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
